<title>GERMANY: German trade seek intervention barley, rye exports.</title>
<headline>German trade seek intervention barley, rye exports.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German traders sought to export 535,188 tonnes of intervention barley and 104,588 tonnes of intervention rye to third countries, intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A BLE source stressed the volumes included multiple bids for identical lots.</p>
<p>The bids were made under the European Union weekly grain tender system.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
